    <item>
      <title>CDC releases tips on how to gather during the holiday season</title>
      <link>https://mytvbuffalo.com/news/cdc-releases-tips-on-how-to-gather-during-the-holiday-season</link>
      <description>Not long after the controversy over Dr. Anthony Fauci’s comments that it may be “too soon to tell” whether families can gather during Christmas, the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention Friday evening released tips on “safer ways to celebrate holidays. ” The guidelines, which were released on Oct. 15, urge eligible individuals to get vaccinated, wear “well-fitting masks,” avoid poorly ventilated and crowded spaces and state that if you are sick “don’t host or attend a gathering. ”</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://mytvbuffalo.com/news/cdc-releases-tips-on-how-to-gather-during-the-holiday-season</guid>
      <enclosure url="https://mytvbuffalo.com/resources/media/647b458c-191f-4680-a23b-a362eff8ff6e-jumbo16x9_AP21089726613959.jpg?1634332890461" length="0" type="image/jpeg"/>
